       attributes  encoding  the character's _r_e_n_d_i_t_i_o_n, such as the styling of
       its typeface and/or foreground and background colors.  See,  for  exam‐
       ple, aaddddcchh(3X), aattttrroonn(3X), and iinncchh(3X).

   _c_c_h_a_r___t,, _a_t_t_r___t
       _c_h_t_y_p_e  is  too small for the standard C library's wide-character type,
       _w_c_h_a_r___t.  _c_c_h_a_r___t is a type that can accommodate an _a_t_t_r___t  and  enough
       wide  characters  to  store  what  Unicode  terms a _g_r_a_p_h_e_m_e _c_l_u_s_t_e_r (a
       “user-perceived character” [UAX #29], which  may  nevertheless  require
